# LegalMind V1 — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (S-6: secrets outside source
# control; keys rotatable). This file lists only variables the code actually
# reads — it invents nothing.
#
# Verify against: backend/legalmind/config.py

# ─── Database (backend/legalmind/config.py) ─────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL is the locked system of record (Step 39, 41.1).
# Databases are named legalmind_v1_* deliberately — see backend/README.md.
LEGALMIND_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@127.0.0.1/legalmind_v1_dev
LEGALMIND_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@127.0.0.1/legalmind_v1_test

# ─── NOT YET SPECIFIED — do not invent these ────────────────────────────────
#
# The following are required by locked decisions but their configuration
# mechanism is explicitly unspecified. Add each variable only when the
# corresponding decision is made — inventing a key name here would make an
# unspecified decision look settled (CLAUDE.md rule 8).
#
#   OIDC provider settings          Step 47 locks OIDC as primary authentication;
#                                   the provider and its client configuration are
#                                   a deployment prerequisite (Step 55.6)
#   Session signing / cookie keys   Step 47 locks server-side sessions; key
#                                   management is NOT YET SPECIFIED
#   Object storage credentials      Step 39 locks S3-compatible storage; the
#                                   provider and layout are NOT YET SPECIFIED
#   Celery / Redis broker URL       locked in the stack table; no code reads it yet
#   Rate-limit thresholds           Step 49: deployment configuration
#   Retention policy settings       NOT YET SPECIFIED (41.26 defers it)

# --- Assist lane (AB-3/AB-4) -------------------------------------------------
# Schema for the assist tables (AM-27 r1). Tests derive a per-run value; deployments
# use the default. LEGALMIND_ASSIST_SCHEMA=assist
# Local embedding-model store (AM-26 r5; weights provisioned once via
# tools/provision_model.py and checksum-verified at load).
# LEGALMIND_MODEL_DIR=/var/lib/legalmind/models
# Generation (AM-30). The key is the ONLY provider secret; never committed, never
# logged. While the AM-31 gate is CLOSED, production egress is refused regardless of
# this key — development/staging (synthetic material only, locked 55.3) will call the
# provider when it is set.
# LEGALMIND_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# A DATED model pin — a floating alias like "-latest" is refused (AM-30 t7).
# LEGALMIND_GENERATION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
